Indeed, we have $\#\mathcal{O}(t)\leq \#(I_t\cap\mathring\mathcal{J}^-)+2\leq \#(I_t\cap\mathcal{J})+2.$ In the setting of $\mathbb{P}_\mathrm{Q}$, using the Poissonian description of $\mathcal{Z}$, by a union bound, for $A>0$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}_\mathrm{Q}\big[\exists\,s\in\mathcal{J}^-:I_s\subseteq I(k), \  \#(I_s\cap\mathcal{J})\geq Ak \big] \leq \mathbb{P}_\mathrm{Q}[\mathcal{J}\cap I(k)\geq 2^{1.1k}] + 2^{1.1k}\big(\frac34\big)^{Ak}\lesssim 2^{-ck^2}+2^{(1.1-A/3)k}.
