  By the same argument, for fixed $R>0$ and each  disk $\check D_{{v}}^{jn}$ in $\check\mathcal{P}^{jn}$  intersects $B(0;R)$, by Theorem~\ref{thm:He-Schramm-sphere}, its diameter tends to 0 in probability,  and  its corresponding disk $D_{{v}}^{jn}$ in $\widetilde\mathcal{P}^{n,j}$ is contained in $B(0;2R)$ with probability tending to 1 as $n\to\infty$. If we write  $\check{o}_{jn}(v)$ for the centers of  $\check D_{{v}}^{jn}$ and $t_v^{jn}$ for the corresponding time in $\mathcal{J}^{jn,-}$, then using \begin{equation}\label{eq:428-pf-a}\sup_{|z|\leq R|\eta(1/j)|}\big|\frac{\varphi(z)}{\varphi(\eta(1/j))} - \frac{ z}{ \eta(1/j)} \big|\to 0  \text{ in probability as }j\to \infty,\end{equation} we also have \begin{equation}\label{eq:CONE-4-new}|\check{o}_{jn}(v) - \frac{\eta(t_v^{jn})}{\eta(1/j)}|\to 0\end{equation} in probability as $n\to\infty$ uniformly over all choices of $v$ such that $\check D_{{v}}^{jn}$  intersects $B(0;R)$. To see this, let $o_{jn}^0(v)$ be the center of the disk for $v$ in $\mathcal{P}^{n,j}$. Then
 \begin{equation*}
